SUMMARY:Amherst Ballet presents The Snow Maiden
LOCATION:HOPE Center for the Arts\, 150 Bridge St\, Springfield\, MA 01103
DESCRIPTION:Amherst Ballet’s beloved winter show\, ‘The Snow Maiden’\
 , returns. This magical production invites you to the land of Father Frost
 \, full of swirling snowflakes and glittering fairies\, where we meet the 
 Snow Maiden on her search for love beyond her wintry realm. Join her quest
  in this heartwarming tale of longing and friendship\, amidst the turning 
 of winter into spring. Set to selections from three works by Peter Tchaiko
 vsky: The Serenade for Strings\, Symphony No. 1 in G-minor (Winter Reverie
 )\, and Incidental Music for the play\, “The Snow Maiden\,” and presen
 ted by students from the Amherst Ballet School and our volunteer company\,
  this production is an excellent opportunity for young audience members to
  experience the magic of ballet for the first time. Several characters fro
 m the show will be available for photographs during intermission\, and our
  director will give backstage tours to show how we bring a production toge
 ther following each show.\nhttps://hopecenterforthearts.org/events/amherst
 -ballet-presents-the-snow-maiden/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://push
 pin.city/westernma/
URL:https://hopecenterforthearts.org/events/amherst-ballet-presents-the-sno
 w-maiden/
